  "why_this_direction": "The same206 negative-component response produced very small best full-objective improvement and mostly collateral response curvature. A small raw component derivative is insufficient to diagnose a coordinate scale issue. Compare an explicitly declared native matrix-scale coordinate hypothesis against the ordinary full gradient at the same held state.",
  "repeating_pattern_check": "Earlier scalar improvement and amplified directions did not establish native derivative fidelity. Compare complete105-term directional responses and physical displacement, not one merge or raw alpha; do not modify training from this read-only result. Earlier inverse-solver preconditioner records indexed in KNOWN.md concern a different withdrawn calculation and do not qualify this coordinate hypothesis; this comparison is motivated and judged by the current retained206 full computational objective.",
  "hypothesis": "Using fixed coordinates Z_m=W_m/sqrt(mean(W_m^2)) for each complete native editable matrix can produce a more useful full-residual direction than raw weight coordinates. This is a new coordinate hypothesis, not a uniquely inferred or already validated metric.",
  "would_weaken_it": "No improvement in full-objective predicted reduction, greater collateral response that erases local gain, or impractically large required relative matrix displacement weakens this coordinate hypothesis. No arbitrary cutoff is used. Any local advantage remains insufficient to establish a native finite or fresh-path improvement.",
